> stream of snakes to spew forth, and my death. sigh.

There are only two circumstances in which it is EVER dipping items in
fountains:

(1) You are wearing a cursed item that you want or need to get rid of
RIGHT NOW (e.g. cursed ring of hunger or levitation), and cannot find
another way of ridding yourself of the item, including praying. (I do
not count "allow a nymph to steal it" as realistic, since nymphs could
steal anything else instead.) You might then take the chance of
getting the message that "The water glows for a moment", which removes
the item's curse.

(2) There is one and only one type of item that is worth dipping into
a fountain for any other reason than to remove the curse. And it isn't
a ring.

(Oh, and (3): There are some items that you might under certain
circumstances want to dip into *water*. A fountain will do: but so
will a pool, and if there's a dry land space by the pool there is no
risk of drowning, and no risk of the side-effects that can occur when
quaffing from or dipping in fountains.)

